    title: "Iran's chief negotiator says there will be 'no more proportionate responses,' and its…",
    lede: "Iran's chief negotiator says there will be 'no more proportionate responses,' and its parliament speaker warns new attacks will meet a 'faster, heavier, more painful' response. The IRGC claims it struck three US-affiliated vessels and three oil tankers today. CENTCOM says it has redirected 92 commercial vessels, disabled 3, and boarded 2. The strait is effectively closed to commercial shipping — 6 vessels/day versus an ~85/day pre-war norm, and war-risk insurance is pricing at 40x peacetime. Brent crude hit $96.28. Witkoff and Kushner's Sep 5 Moscow talks with Putin concluded after three-plus hours with no immediate details announced; Ukrainian drones struck an oil refinery in Ryazan overnight. Russian losses reached 1,496,440 (+1,390) as of Sep 6.",
    body: "Iran's rhetoric shifted sharply today. Chief negotiator and parliament speaker Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf said Tehran would no longer limit itself to 'proportionate responses,' warning that further attacks on Iran would draw a 'faster, heavier, and more painful' reply. Backing that rhetoric, the IRGC claims it attacked three US-affiliated vessels and three oil tankers today using what it called an 'unauthorized' route through the strait. CENTCOM says its blockade-enforcement operations have redirected 92 commercial vessels, disabled three, and boarded two, releasing footage of an F-35A patrol over regional waters. Independent trackers assess the strait as effectively closed to commercial shipping: roughly 6 vessels transited on Aug 30 versus an ~85/day pre-war baseline, and war-risk insurance for tankers is now pricing at roughly 40 times peacetime rates, with six P&I clubs having withdrawn coverage entirely. Analysts at the International Crisis Group suggest Iran may be escalating because it feels its control over the strait — and its main remaining negotiating leverage — slipping away, especially as actual oil transit volumes (nearing 7 million barrels/day by late August) undercut its 'closed strait' narrative. Brent crude has climbed to $96.28/bbl. Separately, US envoys Witkoff and Kushner concluded over three hours of talks with Putin in Moscow on Sep 5 with no immediate details announced on the outcome; Ukrainian drones struck an oil refinery in Ryazan and other Russian targets overnight into Sep 6. On the battlefield, Russian combat losses reached approximately 1,496,440 as of Sep 6 (+1,390), with Ukraine's General Staff recording 245 combat clashes, the heaviest fighting still concentrated on the Pokrovsk and Kostiantynivka axes.",
    watch: "Whether Iran's 'no more proportionate responses' rhetoric translates into a genuinely larger-scale attack rather than continued incremental tanker strikes; whether any details emerge from the Witkoff-Kushner Moscow talks as the delegation reportedly moves toward Kyiv; and whether war-risk insurance costs push shipping companies to abandon the strait route entirely.",
