    title: "CENTCOM declares Hormuz sea lanes mine-free as Iran-Oman agree shipping route",
    lede: "CENTCOM says internationally recognized Hormuz sea lanes are now mine-free — a ‘major milestone’ — with 20-30 tankers/night transiting, about half pre-war volume. Iran and Oman have agreed a shipping route and are finalizing joint-management arrangements, but Tehran insists reopening won't happen until the US ends its own naval blockade. Brent closed Friday at $88.10, down over 5% for the week. Trump announced a sweeping US-Venezuela oil deal — negotiated with acting President Delcy Rodríguez — giving the US access to Venezuela's untapped reserves. Russian losses hit 1,486,600 (+1,400) as of Aug 30. Israel intensified strikes on Hezbollah near Nabatieh's Ali al-Taher ridge.",
